# 0015 XeGfxDisplay: the KMS adapter kext -- an IOFramebuffer driven by the core's KMS KAPI
#
# Base:  none (new files; adapter build b4e22af6)
# Files: kexts/XeGfxDisplay/Info.plist, kexts/XeGfxDisplay/src/XeGfxDisplay.h, kexts/XeGfxDisplay/src/XeGfxDisplay.cpp,
#        kexts/XeGfxDisplay/src/xegfx_kms_kapi.h (all new); built by tools/build-xegfxdisplay.sh (0016)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0015-adapter-xegfxdisplay-kms.patch
#
# The NVRMFB-style end-state framebuffer, matched on XeGfxDisplayNub (0011).  It reads the VBT/child capture and
# the KAPI address from the nub, builds a read-only mode table from getTiming, allocates its scanout through the
# KAPI scanout extension and hands it to the accelerator (xgGetScanoutInfo), forwards presents and vblank queries
# to it (0012), and reports itself to AGDC (0013).  The IntelFB placeholder keeps working beside it; the boot guard
# (0016) decides per boot which one owns the head.
#
